 "notes": [
  "RTT-001 Browser Wars, design pilot 1 (IQ-13, prompts/CODE_SESSION_IQ-13.md). This config is the AS-BUILT reference: values exactly as data/rtt-001/series.csv (straight lines between dated figures, DEC-153), one decimal (metric contract), the house estimated look before January 2009 with the source named on screen (DEC-153), top 10, one logo per browser on a light tile where a usable logo exists (owner direction DEC-180; files listed in logos.json, private), name only otherwise. It is not a film: nothing beyond the approved look goes into a full film before Luke approves it (DEC-069).",
  "The smoothing options A, B and C of DEC-167 are config_rtt001_opt_A/B/C.json (extending this file); the clips and stills extend those. Smoothing is drawn by the player (rtt_timeline.js shareRace); series.csv is never changed.",
  "Drawn by the RTT-002 player (kits/rtt-002) in its series mode with the monthly share kind (race kind 'share', scripts/rtt001_adapter.py). Colours: one per browser (maker_order = browser ids, palette), chosen by DEC-173. No music this round.",
  "Colours (DEC-173): one per browser, near its familiar brand colour; no two browsers that can be on screen together closer than CIEDE2000 18 (closest 18.1, Internet Explorer / Netscape); white names at least 3.0 : 1 on every bar, every bar at least 3.0 : 1 on the background. Browsers that never reach the top 10 get #6E7480 (never drawn). Search: kits/rtt-001/palette_search.js."
 ]
